 "pdCallTexts": [
  {
   "deadId": "gen_q37rkry",
   "entryDay": 21,
   "cause": "the wild",
   "lines": [
    "d21: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Giuseppe Feng is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
    "d21: Nobody's talking much. The fire feels smaller tonight.",
    "d21: 🕯️ Giuseppe Feng is dead — the wild. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging.",
    "d21: What Giuseppe kept close goes into the ground with them — keepsakes are buried, never taken from the body.",
    "d21: \"Giuseppe's gone.\" Yara looks at you for a long moment. \"You're not Giuseppe.\" No heat in it. Just fact. You'll have to earn this face.",
    "d21: The Codex doesn't pause for grief. Zoey blinks — and it's already there, overlaying everything, syncing. No pen. No paper. The mantle just... transfers.",
    "d21: 📖 LEARNED: Animal Behavior (Level 1). Most animals flee. Give them an escape route and they take it. Cornered animals fight.",
    "d21: 📖 LEARNED: Soft Step (Level 1). Move through woods like weather. Less noise, fewer surprises.",
    "d21: 🌟 \"MANTLE TRANSFER DETECTED. ...Oh! New face! Same job! Whole new set of tricks. We hardly noticed. (That is a lie. We noticed. The audience CRIED.)\"",
    "d21: 📖 The Codex turns a page: Giuseppe Feng, 21 days. The mantle passes to Zoey Zuniga.",
    "d21: 🪞 You wake up somebody else. Zoey Zuniga, 43 — an aquarium keeper. Their hands know different work now: Bloodhound.",
    "d21: The village's quarrel was with Giuseppe — and Giuseppe is dead. The sentence doesn't cross the grave. You're someone else now; the docket is empty, but the village remembers.",
    "d21: At the grave, Yara speaks for Zoey — \"Giuseppe trusted them. We saw it. Give them the fire's hearing.\" The village listens.",
    "d21: The fire knew Zoey before the Codex did — their name already carried weight here."
   ]
  },
  {
   "deadId": "gen_pgzt0qk",
   "entryDay": 37,
   "cause": "sickness",
   "lines": [
    "d37: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Zoey Zuniga is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
    "d37: Nobody's talking much. The fire feels smaller tonight.",
    "d37: ZOEY — GONE. 1 open question closed unanswered.",
    "d37: 🕯️ Zoey Zuniga is dead — sickness. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging.",
    "d37: What Zoey kept close goes into the ground with them — keepsakes are buried, never taken from the body.",
    "d37: \"Zoey's gone.\" Manaia looks at you for a long moment. \"You're not Zoey.\" No heat in it. Just fact. You'll have to earn this face.",
    "d37: The Codex doesn't pause for grief. Esperanza blinks — and it's already there, overlaying everything, syncing. No pen. No paper. The mantle just... transfers.",
    "d37: 📖 LEARNED: Tireless Stride (Level 1). You walk like water downhill — no wasted steps, no wasted breath. Every mile costs 15% less.",
    "d37: 📖 LEARNED: Mediation (Level 1). Let each side talk without interruption. Repeat back what you heard. People de-escalate when heard.",
    "d37: 📖 LEARNED: Diplomatic Incident (Level 1). Trust builds 2x faster. You're TOO good though — once per week you can start a diplomatic incident: villagers argue, you pick the winner (+trust with them, -trust with the loser).",
    "d37: 🌟 \"MANTLE TRANSFER DETECTED. ...Oh! New face! Same job! Whole new set of tricks. We hardly noticed. (That is a lie. We noticed. The audience CRIED.)\"",
    "d37: 📖 The Codex turns a page: Zoey Zuniga, 37 days. The mantle passes to Esperanza Schneider.",
    "d37: 🪞 You wake up somebody else. Esperanza Schneider, 56 — a bus driver. Their hands know different work now: Green Whisper.",
    "d37: The village's quarrel was with Zoey — and Zoey is dead. The sentence doesn't cross the grave. You're someone else now; the docket is empty, but the village remembers.",
    "d37: You knew Zoey — not the office, the person. The fire keeps expecting them, and so do you. That's a heavier kind of stepping up. (+5 trauma)",
    "d37: At the grave, Manaia, Pavel, Amina and 2 more speak for Esperanza — \"Zoey trusted them. We saw it. Give them the fire's hearing.\" The village listens.",
    "d37: The fire knew Esperanza before the Codex did — their name already carried weight here."
   ]
  }
 ],
